      "description": "Warehouse racking relocation from Winchester, VA and Martinsburg, WV \u2014 pallet rack teardown and reinstallation, the inventory move that belongs with the steel, storage staging between buildings, industrial equipment disassembly and reassembly, and cubicle and office-systems teardown and reassembly \u2014 surveyed in advance and quoted per job at one flat rate in writing, never by the hour. Racking is torn down, transported, reinstalled and anchored to the floor by the company's crews, to the manufacturer's specification and ANSI MH16.1 / RMI guidance. Where a project requires engineering, seismic calculation or permits, the company consults and arranges them through the certified contractors it engages, so the full scope — any rack type, height or mezzanine configuration — is handled inside the one flat-rate engagement; the engineering and permit authority itself rests with those certified contractors. Components found damaged at teardown are set aside and reported, never re-erected. From Winchester VA and Martinsburg WV, along the I-81, I-66 and I-70 corridors.",
